  // Check for IPv6 addresses first
  const isIPv6 = inputData.sourceIP && inputData.sourceIP.includes(':') && inputData.destinationIP && inputData.destinationIP.includes(':');

  // If input has IPv6 addresses, return Option A
  if (isIPv6) {
    return 'IPv6';
  }

  // Check for HTTP request
  const isHTTPRequest = inputData.port === 80;

  // If input has an HTTP request, return Option B
  if (isHTTPRequest) {
    return 'HTTP';
  }

  // If none of the above, assume UDP (default)
  return 'UDP';
}
```

Note: The `determineMostRelevantProtocol()` function assumes that HTTP requests only happen on port 80, and does not consider other possible ports for HTTPS or custom web servers. It also doesn't take into account payload content or any other application-level protocols. This function is meant to be a simplified example for demonstration purposes.

